    <bp:displayName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">USP17L2 deubiquitinates RCE1</bp:displayName>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref122" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref123" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">USP17L2, also known as USP17, deubiquitinates RCE1 (RAS-converting enzyme 1), inactivating it. Loss of RCE1 activity after USP17L2-mediated deubiquitination interferes with RAS localization and function and prevents downstream signaling through the RAF MAP kinase cascade (Burrows et al, 2009).</bp:comment>
