    <bp:displayName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Mature S-Farn-Me KRAS4B translocates to plasma membrane</bp:displayName>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref239" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref240" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">After farnesylation, C-terminal proteolysis and carboxymethylation, KRAS4B translocates to the plasma membrane (reviewed in Gysin et al, 2011). Localization at the plasma membrane is facilitated by an electrostatic interaction between the polybasic residues in the hypervariable region of KRAS4B and the negatively charged phospholipids of the plasma membrane (Hancock et al, 1990; Yeung et al, 2008).</bp:comment>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#PublicationXref8" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#PublicationXref42" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#PublicationXref43" />
