  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference33">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:P12034-1 FGF5</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FGF5</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref401" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Plays an important role in the regulation of cell proliferation and cell differentiation. Required for normal regulation of the hair growth cycle. Functions as an inhibitor of hair elongation by promoting progression from anagen, the growth phase of the hair follicle, into catagen the apoptosis-induced regression phase (By similarity).SUBUNIT Interacts with FGFR1 and FGFR2. Affinity between fibroblast growth factors (FGFs) and their receptors is increased by heparan sulfate glycosaminoglycans that function as coreceptors.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION Expressed in neonatal brain.DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE Can transform NIH 3T3 cells.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.MISCELLANEOUS Seems to have an antagonistic effect compared to that of the isoform Long.SIMILARITY Belongs to the heparin-binding growth factors family.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
