  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference70">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:O14944 EREG</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">EREG</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref637" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Ligand of the EGF receptor/EGFR and ERBB4. Stimulates EGFR and ERBB4 tyrosine phosphorylation (PubMed:9419975). Contributes to inflammation, wound healing, tissue repair, and oocyte maturation by regulating angiogenesis and vascular remodeling and by stimulating cell proliferation (PubMed:24631357).SUBUNIT Interacts with EGFR and ERBB4.INTERACTION In normal adults, expressed predominantly in the placenta and peripheral blood leukocytes. High levels were detected in carcinomas of the bladder, lung, kidney and colon.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
