  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference73">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q8WWG1 NRG4</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">NRG4</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref648" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Low affinity ligand for the ERBB4 tyrosine kinase receptor. Concomitantly recruits ERBB1 and ERBB2 coreceptors, resulting in ligand-stimulated tyrosine phosphorylation and activation of the ERBB receptors. Does not bind to the ERBB1, ERBB2 and ERBB3 receptors (By similarity).SUBUNIT Interacts with ERBB4.INTERACTION Does not seem to be active.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION The cytoplasmic domain may be involved in the regulation of trafficking and proteolytic processing. Regulation of the proteolytic processing involves initial intracellular domain dimerization (By similarity).DOMAIN ERBB receptor binding is elicited entirely by the EGF-like domain.PTM Proteolytic cleavage close to the plasma membrane on the external face leads to the release of the soluble growth factor form.PTM Extensive glycosylation precedes the proteolytic cleavage.SIMILARITY Belongs to the neuregulin family.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
