  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference88">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:P01135 TGFA</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">TGFA</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref795" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION TGF alpha is a mitogenic polypeptide that is able to bind to the EGF receptor/EGFR and to act synergistically with TGF beta to promote anchorage-independent cell proliferation in soft agar.SUBUNIT Interacts with the PDZ domains of MAGI3, SDCBP and SNTA1. The interaction with SDCBP, is required for the targeting to the cell surface. In the endoplasmic reticulum, in its immature form (i.e. with a prosegment and lacking full N-glycosylation), interacts with CNIH. In the Golgi apparatus, may form a complex with CNIH and GORASP2. Interacts (via cytoplasmic C-terminal domain) with NKD2.INTERACTION Isoform 1, isoform 3 and isoform 4 are expressed in keratinocytes and tumor-derived cell lines.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
