  </bp:Protein>
  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference116">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q13972 RASGRF1</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RASGRF1</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">CDC25</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GNRP</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GRF1</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref977" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Promotes the exchange of Ras-bound GDP by GTP.SUBUNIT Homooligomer and heterooligomer with RASGRF2. Interacts with USP8, thereby regulating its stability (By similarity).ALTERNATIVE PRODUCTS The DH (DBL-homology) domain mediates interaction with RASGRF2.PTM Phosphorylated by PLK2, leading to ubiquitination and degradation by the proteasome.PTM Ubiquitinated and degraded following phosphorylation by PLK2.PTM Phosphorylated by SRC and LCK. Phosphorylation by LCK increases its capacity to stimulate the GDP/GTP exchange on Ras, whereas its phosphorylation by SRC does not seem to have an effect on stimulation activity.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
