    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">IL2RG</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref999" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Common subunit for the receptors for a variety of interleukins. Probably in association with IL15RA, involved in the stimulation of neutrophil phagocytosis by IL15 (PubMed:15123770).SUBUNIT The gamma subunit is common to the IL2, IL4, IL7, IL15, IL21 and probably also the IL13 receptors. Interacts with SHB upon interleukin stimulation. Interacts with IL9 (By similarity).SUBUNIT (Microbial infection) Interacts with HTLV-1 accessory protein p12I.INTERACTION The WSXWS motif appears to be necessary for proper protein folding and thereby efficient intracellular transport and cell-surface receptor binding.DOMAIN The box 1 motif is required for JAK interaction and/or activation.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.SIMILARITY Belongs to the type I cytokine receptor family. Type 5 subfamily.ONLINE INFORMATION X-linked SCID mutation database</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
