  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference122">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:P01589 IL2RA</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">IL2RA</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref1007" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Receptor for interleukin-2. The receptor is involved in the regulation of immune tolerance by controlling regulatory T cells (TREGs) activity. TREGs suppress the activation and expansion of autoreactive T-cells.SUBUNIT Non-covalent dimer of an alpha and a beta subunit. IL2R exists in 3 different forms: a high affinity dimer, an intermediate affinity monomer (beta subunit), and a low affinity monomer (alpha subunit). The high and intermediate affinity forms also associate with a gamma subunit.INTERACTION Disease susceptibility is associated with variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.ONLINE INFORMATION IL2RA mutation db</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
