  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference144">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q9GZZ7 GFRA4</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GFRA4</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref1135" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Receptor for persephin (PSPN), a growth factor that exhibits neurotrophic activity on mesencephalic dopaminergic and motor neurons (PubMed:11116144). Acts by binding to its coreceptor, GFRA4, leading to autophosphorylation and activation of the RET receptor (PubMed:11116144). May be important in C-cell development and, in the postnatal development of the adrenal medulla (PubMed:11116144).SUBUNIT Interacts with ARTN ligand and RET: forms a 2:2:2 ternary complex composed of ARTN ligand, GFRA3 and RET receptor (PubMed:11116144). Interacts with SORL1 (PubMed:23333276).SUBCELLULAR LOCATION Additional isoforms seem to exist.TISSUE SPECIFICITY Predominantly expressed in the adult thyroid gland. Low levels also found in fetal adrenal and thyroid glands.SIMILARITY Belongs to the GDNFR family.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
