    <bp:displayName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RAF phosphorylates MAP2K dimer</bp:displayName>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref1625" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref1626" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Activated RAF phosphorylates the MEK kinases MAP2K1 and MAP2K2 on 2 serine residues in the MAP2K activation loop (S218 and S222 in MAP2K1 and S222 and S226 in MAP2K2 (Zheng and Guan, 1994; Alessi et al, 1994; Catling et al, 1995; Papin et al, 1995; Seger et al, 1994; reviewed in Roskoski, 2012a).  Although all three RAF kinases can phosphorylate MAP2K1 and MAP2K2, BRAF appears to be the primary activator in vivo (Marais et al, 1997; Jaiswal et al, 1994; Pritchard et al, 1995; reviewed in Welbrock et al, 2004)</bp:comment>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#PublicationXref204" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#PublicationXref205" />
