  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference217">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:Q9Y6W6 DUSP10</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">DUSP10</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MKP5</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref1832" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Protein phosphatase involved in the inactivation of MAP kinases. Has a specificity for the MAPK11/MAPK12/MAPK13/MAPK14 subfamily. It preferably dephosphorylates p38.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY O-phospho-L-tyrosyl-[protein] + H2O = L-tyrosyl-[protein] + phosphateCATALYTIC ACTIVITY O-phospho-L-seryl-[protein] + H2O = L-seryl-[protein] + phosphateCATALYTIC ACTIVITY O-phospho-L-threonyl-[protein] + H2O = L-threonyl-[protein] + phosphateSUBUNIT Monomer. Interacts with MAPK14.SUBCELLULAR LOCATION Expressed in keratinocytes (at protein level) (PubMed:29043977). Detected in brain (PubMed:16806267).SIMILARITY Belongs to the protein-tyrosine phosphatase family. Non-receptor class dual specificity subfamily.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
