    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Dual specificity protein phosphatase; active with phosphotyrosine, phosphoserine and phosphothreonine residues. The highest relative activity is toward ERK1.CATALYTIC ACTIVITY O-phospho-L-tyrosyl-[protein] + H2O = L-tyrosyl-[protein] + phosphateCATALYTIC ACTIVITY O-phospho-L-seryl-[protein] + H2O = L-seryl-[protein] + phosphateCATALYTIC ACTIVITY O-phospho-L-threonyl-[protein] + H2O = L-threonyl-[protein] + phosphateINTERACTION Belongs to the protein-tyrosine phosphatase family. Non-receptor class dual specificity subfamily.</bp:comment>
