    <bp:displayName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PTPN7 dephosphorylates ERKs</bp:displayName>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">PTPN7 dephosphorylates p-T,Y-MAPKs</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref1941" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref1942" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Protein tyrosine phosphatase PTPN7 (also known as HePTP) dephosphorylates tyrosine residues of MAPK1 (ERK2) (Saxena et al. 1999, Pettiford and Herbst 2000) and MAPK3 (ERK1) (Saxena et al. 1999), leading to reduction in their catalytic activity.</bp:comment>
