    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION Functions as a Ras GTPase-activating protein. Plays an important role in the expansion and functions of natural killer T (NKT) cells in the liver by negatively regulating RAS activity and the down-stream ERK signaling pathway.INTERACTION Predominantly expressed in cells of hematopoietic lineages.SEQUENCE CAUTION Extended N-terminus.SEQUENCE CAUTION Truncated C-terminus.</bp:comment>
