  <bp:Protein rdf:ID="Protein387">
    <bp:displayName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RASA1</bp:displayName>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Ras GTPase-activating protein 1</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">p120-RasGAP</bp:name>
    <bp:cellularLocation rdf:resource="#CellularLocationVocabulary1" />
    <bp:entityReference rdf:resource="#ProteinReference238" />
    <bp:feature rdf:resource="#FragmentFeature333" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Reactome DB_ID: 186833</bp:comment>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref1990" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref1991" />
    <bp:dataSource rdf:resource="#Provenance1" />
  </bp:Protein>
  <bp:ProteinReference rdf:ID="ProteinReference238">
    <bp:organism rdf:resource="#BioSource1" />
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">UniProt:P20936 RASA1</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RASA1</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">GAP</bp:name>
    <bp:name rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RASA</bp:name>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref1989" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">FUNCTION GTPase-activating protein (GAP) that stimulates the intrinsic GTPase activity of Ras proteins, such as NRAS, facilitating their transition from the active GTP-bound state to the inactive GDP-bound state, thereby terminating Ras signaling.SUBUNIT Interacts with SQSTM1. Interacts with SPSB1; the interaction does not promote degradation. Interacts with CAV2 (tyrosine phosphorylated form). Directly interacts with NCK1. Interacts with PDGFRB (tyrosine phosphorylated). Interacts (via SH2 domain) with the 'Tyr-9' phosphorylated form of PDPK1. Interacts with tyrosine-phosphorylated EPHB4 (PubMed:30578106).INTERACTION In placental villi, detected only in the trophoblast layer (cytotrophoblast and syncytiotrophoblast). Not detected in stromal, endothelial or Hofbauer cells (at protein level).PTM The N-terminus is blocked.PTM Phosphorylated by SRC and LCK. The phosphorylation SRC inhibits its ability to stimulate the Ras-GTPase activity, whereas phosphorylation by LCK does not display any effect on stimulation activity.DISEASE Mutations in the SH2 domain of RASA seem to be oncogenic and cause basal cell carcinomas.DISEASE The disease is caused by variants affecting the gene represented in this entry.</bp:comment>
  </bp:ProteinReference>
