    <bp:displayName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">RAS GAPs stimulate RAS GTPase activity</bp:displayName>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref2020" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref2021" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">The intrinsic GTPase activity of RAS proteins is stimulated by the GAP proteins, of which there are at least 10 in the human genome (reviewed in King et al, 2013).</bp:comment>
