    <bp:eCNumber rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2.7.11.9</bp:eCNumber>
    <bp:displayName rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MAP2K1 phosphorylates MAPK3</bp:displayName>
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref2235" />
    <bp:xref rdf:resource="#UnificationXref2236" />
    <bp:comment rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">MAP2K1 (also known as MEK1) phosphorylates the critical Thr202 and Tyr204 on MAPK3 (ERK1), converting two ATP to ADP. Phosphorylation of MAPK3 activates its kinase activity.&lt;p&gt;MAP2K1 activation requires the phosphorylation of two serine residues (S218 and S222) in the activation loop.</bp:comment>
